course: dictionary
lesson: 15152
title: Old words for everyday places
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name places that have changed over time. A schoolroom is a room where children are taught. «The schoolroom in the old house had wooden desks and a big black stove.» The word tells you the room was for lessons, and the old house is a clue that this was a long time ago.
explain: Look inside the word: school and room. A school is where you learn, and a room is one space inside a building. Put them together and you get a room for school. Can you guess what a bedroom is for?
explain: Context helps you see how a word is used. «Long ago, the governess taught the rich children in the schoolroom at the top of the house.» A governess was a teacher who lived with the family. Today we usually say classroom for the same kind of room.
fact: A schoolroom is a room where children are taught.
fact: Schoolroom is a noun. You can have one schoolroom or many schoolrooms.
fact: Long ago, rich families often had a schoolroom at home, where a governess taught the children.
fact: Village schools once had one schoolroom for children of all ages.
fact: Today we usually say «classroom» instead of «schoolroom».
exercise: «The schoolroom was full of wooden desks and a big clock on the wall.» What is a schoolroom? | A kitchen where food is cooked | A large garden with trees | A shop that sells books | *A room where children are taught
exercise: «Long ago, rich children learned their lessons in a schoolroom at home.» What do we usually call a schoolroom today? | Bedroom | Playroom | Kitchen | *Classroom
exercise: «Alice thought of the schoolroom as she chanted her times tables.» Where did Alice learn her tables? | *In a room where children are taught | At a café | At the beach | In the park
test: «The schoolroom at the top of the house was cold and quiet.» Where was the schoolroom? | In the garden | *At the top of the house | Under the sea | In a shop
test: «Some village schools had one schoolroom for children of all ages.» What does this tell you? | Schools had no teachers | *Children of different ages were taught together | Only the oldest children went to school | Children were only taught at home
exam: Which sentence uses schoolroom correctly? | She schoolroomed her dinner in the garden. | We swam in the schoolroom pond. | *We learned our spellings in the schoolroom. | The schoolroom was delicious for lunch.
